# Tools

## file_read
Read a file from disk. Returns the file's content with 1-indexed line numbers. Use offset/limit to read a slice. Image files (PNG/JPG/GIF/WebP) are returned as a base64 attachment with the correct mime type.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "file_path" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Absolute path to the file to read."
    },
    "offset" : {
      "type" : "integer",
      "description" : "Optional 0-indexed line offset. Omit to read from the start."
    },
    "limit" : {
      "type" : "integer",
      "description" : "Optional max number of lines to return. Omit to read the whole file."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "file_path" ]
}
```

## file_write
Write a file. Replaces the existing content. Refuses to write outside the current working directory unless AETHERCODE_ALLOW_ANY_PATH=1.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "file_path" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Absolute path of the file to write."
    },
    "content" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "The new content of the file."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "file_path", "content" ]
}
```

## file_edit
Edit a file by replacing a unique snippet. Returns a diff for the UI.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "file_path" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Absolute path of the file to edit."
    },
    "old_string" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "The exact text to replace. Must match a unique location unless replace_all is true."
    },
    "new_string" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "The replacement text."
    },
    "replace_all" : {
      "type" : "boolean",
      "description" : "If true, replace every occurrence of old_string. Default: false."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "file_path", "old_string", "new_string" ]
}
```

## glob
List files matching a glob. Recursive, sorted, capped at 200 results by default.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "pattern" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Glob pattern, e.g. '**/*.java' or 'src/**/pom.xml'."
    },
    "base_dir" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Optional base directory. Defaults to the working directory."
    },
    "max_results" : {
      "type" : "integer",
      "description" : "Optional cap. Defaults to 200."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "pattern" ]
}
```

## grep
Recursively grep a directory for a regex. Returns path:line:content. Cap 200 by default.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "pattern" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Java regular expression."
    },
    "base_dir" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Optional base directory. Defaults to the working directory."
    },
    "include" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Optional file glob to include, e.g. '*.java'."
    },
    "max_results" : {
      "type" : "integer",
      "description" : "Optional cap. Defaults to 200."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "pattern" ]
}
```

## bash
Run a shell command. Returns stdout, stderr, and exit code. Default timeout 30s. R19-G: streams output line-by-line and respects abort signals. Set background=true to run detached (returns job id).
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "command" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Shell command to run."
    },
    "timeout_ms" : {
      "type" : "integer",
      "description" : "Optional timeout in milliseconds. Default 180 000 (3 min)."
    },
    "cwd" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Optional working directory. Default: current directory."
    },
    "stream" : {
      "type" : "boolean",
      "description" : "R19-G: if true, stream each output line as a progress message (default true). Set false to suppress progress emission and only see the final captured output."
    },
    "background" : {
      "type" : "boolean",
      "description" : "R19-G: if true, run the command in the background. Returns a job ID immediately; the process keeps running. Use /jobs to inspect or /job-kill <id> to stop."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "command" ]
}
```

## todo_write
Update the in-session todo list. The full new list is sent on every call. Each top-level todo may carry a `subtasks[]` field for finer-grained business units the engine tracks separately.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "todos" : {
      "type" : "array",
      "description" : "The full new state of the todo list.",
      "items" : {
        "type" : "object",
        "properties" : {
          "content" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Short description."
          },
          "status" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "One of: pending, in_progress, completed, cancelled, skipped."
          },
          "active_form" : {
            "type" : "string",
            "description" : "Present-tense form shown to the user."
          },
          "subtasks" : {
            "type" : "array",
            "description" : "Optional sub-tasks (business-concept units) under this top-level todo.",
            "items" : {
              "type" : "object",
              "properties" : {
                "id" : {
                  "type" : "string",
                  "description" : "Stable identifier. Reuse the same id across calls."
                },
                "content" : {
                  "type" : "string",
                  "description" : "Short description of this business unit."
                },
                "status" : {
                  "type" : "string",
                  "description" : "One of: pending, in_progress, completed, failed, skipped."
                },
                "summary" : {
                  "type" : "string",
                  "description" : "Optional one-line summary written when the sub-task closes."
                }
              },
              "required" : [ "id", "content", "status" ]
            }
          }
        },
        "required" : [ "content", "status" ]
      }
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "todos" ]
}
```

## sub_todo_write
Incrementally update a single sub-task (status / summary) without re-sending the full todo list. Cheaper than todo_write for closing a sub-task and writing its summary.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "parent_index" : {
      "type" : "integer",
      "description" : "0-based index of the parent top-level todo in the current todo list."
    },
    "subtask_id" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Stable id matching the sub-task in the parent's subtasks[] array."
    },
    "status" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "New status. One of: pending, in_progress, completed, failed, skipped."
    },
    "summary" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Optional one-line summary written when the sub-task closes (typically set together with status=completed/failed/skipped)."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "parent_index", "subtask_id" ]
}
```

## spawn_agent
Spawn a subagent. The subagent has its own task ID (visible in /tasks). Default mode (multi_step=false) is a single LLM call with no tool use — good for summarising a file, drafting a doc, asking a focused question. Set multi_step=true to let the subagent call tools; it will share the parent's tool pool, system prompt, and transcript context. Recursion is bounded to 2 levels. R89-J: pass a 'role' to pick a specialised subagent preset (explore / general-purpose / coder). R90-D: pass background=true to fire-and-forget; the tool returns a job id immediately and the subagent runs on a daemon thread.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "prompt" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "The task the subagent should perform. Keep it self-contained."
    },
    "context" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "Optional short summary of the parent's work so far (helps the subagent stay on track)."
    },
    "multi_step" : {
      "type" : "boolean",
      "description" : "If true, the subagent can call tools (read files, run bash, etc.) and runs the full engine loop. Default false (single-shot, text-only)."
    },
    "role" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "R89-J role preset: 'explore' (read-only), 'general-purpose' (default), 'coder' (write-focused, no web)."
    },
    "background" : {
      "type" : "boolean",
      "description" : "R90-D: if true, the subagent runs in the background. The tool returns a job id immediately; use subagent_status to poll."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "prompt", "multi_step" ]
}
```

## subagent_status
Get the status of a background subagent. Returns 'running', 'completed: <text>', 'failed: <error>', or 'cancelled'. Use subagent_list to see all jobs.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : {
    "job_id" : {
      "type" : "string",
      "description" : "The subagent job id returned by spawn_agent(background=true)."
    }
  },
  "required" : [ "job_id" ]
}
```

## subagent_list
List all subagent jobs the engine knows about (running + recently finished). Each line is one job in the same format as subagent_status.
Input schema:
```json
{
  "type" : "object",
  "properties" : { }
}
```

## web_fetch
